Title: The Last Biscuit
Credit: A play in one act by
Author: Lexington's examples
Draft date: October 2026

# ACT ONE

.SCENE 1

A kitchen. Morning. A tin of biscuits on the table, its lid off. ANNA enters, sees the tin and stops.

ANNA
(to herself)
One left. Just one.

She reaches for it. BRAM enters from the garden, muddy.

BRAM
Don't you dare.

ANNA
I was here first, Bram. I have been waiting for this biscuit since breakfast, and I will not give it up to someone who has been digging up the roses all morning.

BRAM
(holding up a trowel)
Planting. There is a difference.

They both look at the tin. Lights fade.

> BLACKOUT.

.SCENE 2

The same kitchen, that evening. The tin is empty.
